5,1,1,talk,Rin,,Hi everyone! I don't like how smelly and icky the corner gets in August. Can we find out what it's actually like to live next to the bins in other places?,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree, Rin. It's important to see how others handle it. I'm also worried about the costs. We should check the block ledger of refuse-point expenses and the ward subsidy to see what we can afford.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,Let's not forget that the smell isn't the only thing rotting here. We should check the ward complaint log for this point to see exactly who is upset and why. It's better to face the facts.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,"I'm with you all, but let's be real—who's actually doing the work? I want to see the supervised mornings on the next lane and the station block's meeting minutes to see how much time this takes.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Asuka,,We need objective data to ensure fairness. I suggest we look into the measurements of the five frontages and the ward filing requirements per the installations clerk to understand the physical and legal constraints.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, that's a great idea! If we see how other people do it, maybe we can find a way to make it not icky. I want to see the bin house at the station block too!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that sounds like a wonderful way to get inspiration. I still feel we need a clear picture of our finances first, so I'll stick with the ledger and the subsidy information to keep us grounded.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, grounding us in numbers is fine, but numbers don't fix grudges. I'll also look into the statements at the residents' meeting. I want to know the actual tone of the arguments we're trying to resolve.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're so dramatic! But you're right, the ""vibe"" matters. Still, I'm more worried about the actual labor. I'll stick with my plan to check the minutes and those supervised mornings. No one wants a second job for free.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, labor is important, but spatial burden is a constant. If the site remains in one spot, the burden isn't shared. I will proceed with the frontage measurements and the filing requirements to ensure any new plan is equitable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Rin,,I wonder if the truck drivers have any secrets! Maybe they know a better spot? I'll check the truck arrival time from the crew leader and the visit to the station block's bin house!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that's a very creative idea! I hope the crew leader has some helpful tips. I'll stay focused on the block ledger and the ward subsidy so we can make sure the costs are fair for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, chasing the truck drivers is a bit optimistic, isn't it? I'll stick with the complaint log and the residents' meeting statements. Let's see if we can find the root of the bitterness before we move the bins.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,"@Rin, you're adorable, but let's not get distracted by truck driver secrets! I'm staying focused on the labor. I'll stick with the supervised mornings and the meeting minutes. I'm not letting any of us become an unpaid servant.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, it is not about being a servant, but about the physical reality of the space. I will stick with the measurements of the five frontages and the ward filing requirements. We cannot ignore the spatial impact.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Rin,,I'm excited! I'll find out about the truck times and the bin house. I hope we can make our corner a happy place to walk past again! See you all after the research!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Midori,,I'm looking forward to seeing what we all find. I really hope we can find a solution that is both effective and affordable for every household. See you all soon!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's hope the data is more cooperative than we've been. I'll see if the records reveal any patterns we can actually work with. Until then, try not to start any new wars over the bins.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,"Good luck with your little treasure hunts, everyone! I'll be the one making sure we don't accidentally sign our lives away to the bin gods. See you all in a bit!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Asuka,,I will focus on the facts. I hope the measurements and requirements provide a clear basis for a truly equitable distribution of the burden. I will see you all once the information is gathered.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
