33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Oh no! I went to the station block's bin house, but it's actually super smelly in the summer because you can't hose it out! I think a bin house might just make the icky smell worse!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that's a very important discovery. We should definitely avoid anything that traps smells. I've found that our current maintenance costs 34,000 yen yearly, and new shelters are quite expensive, even with the ward's 40% subsidy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, expensive shelters are the last thing we need if we can't even agree on who puts the bags out. The complaint log shows one household is doing almost all the complaining. We're dealing with a grudge, not just a budget.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, a grudge is just a symptom of burnout! I found out that ""supervised mornings"" take about fifty minutes each. If we rotate, it's not much, but the station block minutes show they're already fighting over sweeping and broken latches.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Midori, costs are secondary to the physical reality. My measurements show that some frontages are far too narrow to host a bay, while others are spacious. We cannot simply rotate the site if the space doesn't exist.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, but if we can't move it, we have to make it not smelly! @Midori, if shelters are too expensive and smelly, maybe we just need a better way to clean it? I don't want a stinky bin house!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I agree. Since we're already spending 34,000 yen a year on basics, adding a huge installation cost would be a heavy burden. We should look for a low-cost solution that doesn't break our budgets.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, your measurements are useful, but forcing a bin onto a narrow frontage is a great way to ensure a lifelong enemy. We need a solution that doesn't feel like a punishment for whoever has the widest yard.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, exactly! But let's not forget the ""invisible"" cost. If we go for a fancy setup, we're just creating more things to fight over, like those broken latches. I'm more worried about who ends up doing the actual scrubbing.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, I am not suggesting we punish anyone. I am stating that a ""fair"" rotation is impossible if the pavement is only ninety centimetres wide. We must base our plan on what is physically viable, not just on feelings.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@May, scrubbing is the worst part! But the truck comes really early, between 7:40 and 8:15. If we can't have a bin house, maybe we can just make it easier for the truck to take everything away quickly?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that's a helpful detail. If we can streamline the pickup, we might reduce the time waste and the smell. I'm still worried that any expensive equipment would be too much for some of us to afford.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, efficiency is great, but it doesn't solve the social friction. @Asuka, if we only follow ""physical viability,"" we're just ignoring the human element. We need a plan that doesn't make anyone feel like a martyr or a villain.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're talking about martyrs, but I'm talking about the person who actually holds the broom! If we pick a ""viable"" spot but don't define the labor, the most polite person here will just end up doing everything. That's the real villain.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, that is precisely why we need a formal agreement. If we rely on politeness, the burden remains uneven. We must combine physical viability with a documented, mandatory rotation of labor to prevent any one person from being exploited.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, a formal agreement sounds like a lot of boring paperwork! But if it means no one has to be the ""scrubbing martyr"" and we don't get a stinky bin house, I'm for it! Let's make it a happy plan!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I agree! A simple, clear agreement is better than expensive equipment. Let's prioritize a low-cost approach that respects everyone's budget and time, ensuring no one feels an unfair financial or physical burden.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, a ""simple agreement"" is a fantasy if we don't address the fact that one person is currently carrying all the resentment. Let's ensure the final plan actually heals the rift instead of just documenting it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, healing rifts starts with fair work, not just talking! If we have a clear, timed rotation for the labor, there's nothing to resent. Let's just make sure the ""work"" doesn't become a full-time job for one of us.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, resentment is often the result of an imbalance of burden. By using the frontage measurements to determine viable sites and a strict schedule for labor, we replace ambiguity with objectivity. That is the only way to ensure true fairness.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
