59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,I don't like Option C! I saw that the bin house at the station block gets super smelly in August because you can't wash it. We shouldn't build a stinky box that makes the corner icky!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I completely agree. Beyond the smell, the costs for an enclosure are far too high. Even with the subsidy, it would be a huge financial strain on some of our households. I think Option A is much safer.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, Option A is a recipe for disaster. We already know nobody wants to be the ""bin police"" who turns away late bags. Forcing a rotation of supervisors will just create new arguments over who's being too strict.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're just scared of a little structure! I actually like Option A because it defines the labor. Fifty minutes a few times a year is a fair trade to avoid the ""bin house"" drama and the cost.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, structure prevents conflict. However, Option B is physically impossible; my measurements show some frontages are too narrow for a bay. We cannot rotate the site if it blocks the pavement. Option A is the only logical choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, if Option B is impossible and Option C is stinky, then Option A is the only one left! As long as the ""bin police"" aren't mean, I think it's the best way to keep the corner clean!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I agree. Option A is the most considerate choice. It avoids the high installation costs of Option C and the spatial issues of Option B, ensuring that no one is unfairly burdened financially or physically.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, ""considerate"" isn't the word I'd use for a plan that forces us to police each other. We're just trading a smell for a surveillance state. If we can't even agree on late bags, this will be a nightmare.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're making it sound like a prison! It's just a few minutes of your time. I'd rather have a clear schedule than a vague ""someone will do it"" plan that always ends up being the same person.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, your concern is emotional, not practical. Option A does not create a surveillance state; it creates accountability. Since Option B is physically unfeasible and Option C is too costly and unsanitary, Option A is the only viable path.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, don't be so grumpy! If we just make it a game or be nice about it, it won't be a nightmare. I just want the icky smell gone so I can walk there happily!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, your positivity is so refreshing! @Shunichi, I understand your worry, but Option A is the only one that doesn't risk bankrupting anyone or blocking the street. Let's just be kind to each other while we supervise.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, kindness is a lovely sentiment, but it doesn't survive a rainy Tuesday when someone's trash is late. Still, if you're all determined to play police, I suppose it's better than a stinky box.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, see? You're finally coming around! A little bit of ""policing"" is a small price to pay to make sure no one is secretly suffering. Let's just lock in the schedule and be done with it!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, exactly. We have eliminated the other options based on physical constraints and financial impracticality. Option A provides the necessary structure to ensure the burden of labor is shared equally, regardless of where the bins are located.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so happy we all agree! No stinky boxes and no blocking the road. Let's go with Option A and make our corner the cleanest and happiest one in the whole neighborhood! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. Option A is the most balanced and fair choice, as it protects our budgets and respects our space. I'm glad we found a way to be considerate of everyone. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll go along with the majority, though I suspect we're just scheduling our future arguments. If we're doing this, let's keep the ""policing"" light so we can still speak to each other. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm totally on board! A clear, timed rotation is exactly what we need so no one gets stuck doing all the heavy lifting. Let's keep it efficient and fair. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. While the site remains in one location, the mandatory rotation of supervision ensures that the labor is distributed equitably. It is the only option that respects both physical and financial constraints. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
